doc pkc: the Packenger compiler, written in Packenger.
  The self-hosted compiler, ported module by module from the Go compiler
  and checked against it by the comparison harness
  ([docs/dumps.md](../dumps.md#the-comparison-harness)). Build it with the
  Go compiler, then let it build itself:

  ```sh
  packenger build bootstrap/pkc.pkg -o pkc
  PKC=$PWD/pkc go test ./bootstrap/
  ```

  Its packages use short prefixes, since library names share one
  namespace: `u_` (util), `fe_` (fetch), `pf_` (package files), `lx_`
  (lexer), `lg_` (grammar), `dr_` (driver), `ui_` (errors and the build
  report) and `pkc_` (the command line).

